  "$comment": "R02 test catalog. Every scripts/_test-*.ts must appear here exactly once (run-tests.mjs --check enforces it in CI). `helper` = imported by other tests, never run on its own. Lanes: unit | db | scheduler | browser | manual. See docs/titanor-time/TEST_CATALOG_RU.md.",
  "lanes": {
    "unit": "No database, no browser. Pure functions or mocked globals (fake-indexeddb, mocked fetch/caches). Runs anywhere, no env.",
    "db": "Needs a disposable PostgreSQL 16 with every migration applied. Direct route-handler / lib calls — no HTTP server. run-tests.mjs gives each test its own fresh database cloned from a migrated template.",
    "scheduler": "Same runtime as `db`, but the subject under test is a scheduler tick / horizon / auto-close pass. Run together with the db lane.",
    "browser": "Needs a running standalone server (TEST_BASE_URL) and usually Chromium (playwright). Not part of the unattended CI gate — runs at pilot acceptance (R12 / TZ 18.2 item 10).",
    "manual": "Excluded from every automated gate. See the per-test note for why and how to run it."
  },
